    "sourceWikitext": "{{recipe summary|\n| category = Chicken recipes\n| servings = 4\n| Difficulty = 2\n| time = 30 minutes\n}}{{recipe}}\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 400 [[Cookbook:Gram|grams]] (about 1 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]]) boneless [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] meat, [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] chicken [[Cookbook:Stock|stock]]\n* 100 grams (3.5 oz) straw [[Cookbook:Mushroom|mushrooms]], halved \n* 6 cherry [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n* 1 fresh [[Cookbook:Lemongrass|lemongrass]] stem, cut into short lengths\n* 2–3 [[Cookbook:Kaffir Lime Leaf|kaffir lime leaves]], torn\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] Thai [[Cookbook:Fish Sauce|fish sauce]]\n* 4 tbsp fresh [[Cookbook:Lime|lime]] juice\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 5–6 hot fresh Thai [[Cookbook:Chiles|chilies]], just broken with [[Cookbook:Mortar and Pestle|pestle]] \n==Procedure==\n#Place the stock in a pot, add the lemongrass and kaffir lime leaves, and bring to [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] over medium heat.\n#Add the chicken meat, mushroom, fish sauce, lime juice, and sugar; cook slowly and uncovered for 10 minutes. Do not stir.\n#Add the tomatoes and chilies and cook for 5 more minutes. Remove from heat.\n#Serve with steamed jasmine rice.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using straw mushroom]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Thai recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Soup recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using Thai chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lime juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fish sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using kaffir lime]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemongrass]]",
    "isRecipe": true,
